Multi-page html static output: each filename derives from that page's
folded href, not from its id and not from a source-line fallback. The
golden's file set is the assertion -- an `out/none/html/window_L1.html` would
be an extra file, and the harness compares the set both ways.

The pages are a nav.stack's, and the window around the stack is the shell
every document shares; its title is the page's.

-- site.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"
import nav "sngl:ui/nav"

output { none { html } }

window(title=pages.current.title) {
    nav.stack #pages {
        nav.page #home(href="/", title="Home") { text(value="home") }
        nav.page #about(href="/about.html", title="About") { text(value="about") }
        nav.page #intro(href="/docs/intro.html", title="Intro") { text(value="intro") }
    }
}
-- out/none/html/about.html --
